  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of protective environment and lifesaving assistance to mitigate the impact of violence and other protection threats against vulnerable individuals and communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project aims to reduce protection risks and strengthen the resilience of vulnerable individuals in Laas Qoray District, Sanaag, including women, men, children, the elderly, persons with disabilities, and other marginalized groups. Recurrent conflict-related displacement, drought-induced migration, and ongoing economic shocks have increased exposure to abuse, exploitation, and violence, while limited access to formal protection services leaves many individuals without support. The project will directly target 1,000 vulnerable individuals with heightened protection needs, prioritizing women and girls at risk of GBV, unaccompanied or separated children, persons with disabilities, older persons, and minority community members. Through mobile outreach and static protection desks, the project will deliver comprehensive services including Individual Protection Assistance (IPA), protection case management for non-child protection and GBV cases, psychosocial support, protection awareness and sensitization, and facilitated referrals to specialized service providers. In addition, the project will establish community-led protection structures and strengthen local self-protection mechanisms to identify and support at-risk individuals, enhance early-warning capacities, and promote safer community environments. By integrating targeted outreach, capacity-building for local actors, and inclusive protection programming, the project seeks to mitigate negative coping strategies, increase access to life-saving services, and improve the overall protective environment for vulnerable individuals in Laas Qoray District.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
